--- Finding (distance_and_bearing): math's atan2 of two plain numbers is refused before the
--- program runs, in both modes, while every one-argument trig function takes a plain
--- number (sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan each have a number row beside the tensor row;
--- atan2 has only `(Tensor, Tensor) -> Tensor`, src/table.rs "math.atan2"). The spec
--- writes atan2 as sin is written ("Element-wise two-argument arctangent"), and the
--- message reads as if it were given the wrong kind ("numbers" and "a number").
---
--- crow run -i and crow run (both):
---     line 16:5: atan2[] takes numbers and numbers, got a number and a number
--- Expected: 0.7853981633974483 (as math.atan2(1.0, 1.0) in Python, and as
---     atan2[[1.0], [1.0]][0] prints in both modes, which is the workaround)
--- (a04's averages_mean_angle met it too and noted it in its status line.)
use math
log[sin[1.0]]
log[asin[0.5]]
log[atan2[1.0, 1.0]]
